"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Enumerations","anchor":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/FlushOutcome"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules","anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Foundation"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"collection","title":"Swidux","externalID":"Swidux","symbolKind":"module"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"Swidux-logo"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is a Redux-style state-management library for SwiftUI. State lives in one observable store, mutations go through reducers, and side effects run as async effects. Macros generate the observability boilerplate. Built-in plugins handle persistence and undo\/redo. Optional plugins ship ready-made paywalls (RevenueCat or StoreKit-shaped), version killswitches, parental gates, analytics (Mixpanel or any backend), feature flags, and SwiftData\/iCloud persistence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The dispatch cycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["View → store.send(.action)","  → willReduce hooks (UndoPlugin snapshots here)","  → reducer mutates state in place, optionally returns Effect","  → plugin reducers handle their own actions","  → afterReduce hooks (PersistencePlugin drains EntityStore changelogs here)","  → observer tree updates only changed properties (per-property observation)","  → effects run on a background actor; results dispatch back via @MainActor send"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your domain types and database stay in your app. Swidux provides the contracts, observability, and dispatch loop."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Companion-Packages","text":"Companion Packages","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-specific adapters live in their own repositories so a third-party SDK never enters the core dependency graph. Each ships a drop-in service conformer plus a preview mock, and publishes its own DocC reference:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/"},{"text":" — RevenueCat adapter for the paywall plugin (","type":"text"},{"code":"RevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sheet). See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/"},{"text":" — Mixpanel adapter for the analytics plugin (","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documen